  <verbatim|hinge_transport>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Ends.lean>,
  <verbatim|Wire.lean>, <verbatim|Signal.lean>,
  <verbatim|Scripts.lean>>|<cell|The prose checks the ingredients used by the
  actual wire's two-form script shift. It does not use the tabE/weights
  computation from the separate scriptA shift.>>>>>

  <section|Wire branch producer ledger><label|wire-branch-producer-ledger>

  <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.wire_budget> is not an axiom or a type-level
  record assumption: it is a proof. Its two branch theorems are:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.copper_budget>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Cable.lean>: the zero-alias term. The
    proof combines the foot and flux product, then the brace/latch/mouth
    product and pulse/latch/tail correction, multiplies by the dual exterior
    multiplier, and adds the estimates.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.stake_budget>, same path: the
    nonzero-alias term. The proof combines the
    heart/signal/port-mask/flux/dual-multiplier product and the
    levy/flux/notch product, then adds them. The alias weight is preserved or
    weakened by the grade bounds.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.wire_budget>, same path: partitions
    the alias site into zero and nonzero cases and invokes the two branch
    estimates.
  </itemize-minus>

  The directly invoked component estimates include <verbatim|latch_budget>,
  <verbatim|mouth_budget>, <verbatim|foot_budget>, <verbatim|brace_budget>,
  <verbatim|copper_budget>, <verbatim|notch_budget>, <verbatim|levy_budget>,
  <verbatim|stake_budget>, and <verbatim|wire_budget> in
  <verbatim|Cable.lean>. The products further use <verbatim|flux_budget>,
  <verbatim|sig_budget>, <verbatim|portD_budget>, and <verbatim|tail_budget>
  from <verbatim|Buffer.lean>; <verbatim|heart_budget> from
  <verbatim|Heart.lean>; and train bend, bulb, rail, mass, denominator, and
  alias controls from the adjoining files. The source proof uses the closure
  operations on <verbatim|Pay> and <verbatim|Moderate> (sum, product,
  scaling, transpose/reversal, reciprocal under a proved lower bound, and
  finite branches). The two article chapters reconstruct the lower
  train-factor inequalities and the branch identities; their precise source
  crosswalk is in <verbatim|free-kernel-components-evidence.md>.

  <section|Correspondence of the article proof><label|correspondence-of-the-article-proof>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Article
  statement>>|<cell|<strong|Formal correspondence>>|<cell|<strong|Classification>>>|<row|<cell|Lemma
  <verbatim|lem:ex-lattice-uniform-strip-extraction>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.tapes_sound>;
  analytic coefficient estimate <verbatim|YM.Laurent.Vane.issues>;
  <verbatim|YM.Work.F07.widthRealPart>>|<cell|New direct Cauchy-contour
  derivation of the same type of estimate, using a common smaller strip and
  explicit product geometric sum>>|<row|<cell|Bound
  <math|<big|sum><rsub|l\<in\>\<Lambda\><rsub|L>>\<Gamma\><rsub|L><around|(|l|)><rsup|-2>\<leqslant\>81>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.decay_cost>>|<cell|Article
  proves a concrete dimension-four bound using the one-dimensional integral
  test>>|<row|<cell|Word factor and alias average estimate (equations
  <verbatim|ex-lattice-spread-symbol>\U<verbatim|ex-lattice-spread-supremum>)>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.differential_bound>,
  <verbatim|residue_cost>, and <verbatim|Secured.propels>>|<cell|Reorganized
  quantitative argument; the source uses Pay/Moderate closure to obtain the
  same <math|L<rsup|-<around|(|e+s|)>>> price>>|<row|<cell|Lemma
  <verbatim|lem:ex-lattice-residue-difference>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.enters>
  and <verbatim|Secured.traverse>, based on
  <verbatim|Precision.forwardC>>|<cell|Article derives the exact carry phase
  and checks the Fourier reindexing>>|<row|<cell|Theorem
  <verbatim|thm:ex-lattice-wire-tower-strip>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Secured.bankCost>,
  <verbatim|.traverse>, <verbatim|.honored>; <verbatim|Flight.duo>;
  downstream <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.pledges>>|<cell|Article proves strip
  extraction after deriving the wire bound and overlap data in the companion
  component calculation>>>>>

  The standard analytic inputs are the one-variable Cauchy integral theorem,
  identity theorem, and Fourier uniqueness for an absolutely convergent
  Fourier series on the torus. The chapter states and checks the contour
  movement and geometric summation explicitly. No outside RG theorem is used.

  <section|Literature and source search><label|literature-and-source-search>

  The shared background-note search for <verbatim|Wilson>, <verbatim|atlas>,
  <verbatim|Schur>, <verbatim|kernel>, <verbatim|strip>, <verbatim|Laurent>,
  and <verbatim|RG> found only <verbatim|blueprint/background/su2-simplicity.md>,
  which does not cover these Fourier-strip estimates. No relevant external
  result was needed: the exact contour shift and lattice sum are proved in
  the chapter. The nearest source implementation of the analytic coefficient
  extraction is <verbatim|YM.Laurent.Vane.issues>, whose hypotheses (bounded
  holomorphic function on a periodic strip) match the smaller-width
  formulation given here.

  <section|Commands and limits><label|commands-and-limits>

  Read-only inspection commands included:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,140p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/MatrixPay.lean>
    \V definitions of weighted payments, finite product/sum closure, and the
    entrywise-to-matrix cover extractor.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,140p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/AliasWeights.lean>
    \V the centered-lift polynomial weight, absorption inequality, and
    uniform residue sum.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,150p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Cable.lean> \V
    the wire estimate and its zero/nonzero branch proofs.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,175p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Strands.lean>
    and <verbatim|sed -n '1,135p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Sprout.lean> \V
    finite-difference symbol and the complete strip receipt extraction to all
    word lengths.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,230p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Glue.lean>,
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,120p' Lean/YM/Laurent/Art.lean>, and <verbatim|sed -n
    '1,145p' Lean/YM/Work/F07/Read.lean> \V overlap gluing, Cauchy
    coefficient majorant, and real-coefficient extraction.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,120p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Wire.lean> and
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,175p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Buffer.lean> \V dual
    kernel definition and immediately used weighted component estimates.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,180p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Feed.lean> \V
    pull-line and drive factors; finite normalized feed, mixed-radix
    reindexing, train noise and level-response feedback.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,220p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Scripts.lean>
    \V exact definitions of the two-form script and its scalar branch inputs.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '70,185p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Wire.lean> \V
    zero and nonzero branch matching equations and the helper identities used
    by them.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '70,112p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Ends.lean> \V
    reciprocal shift of <verbatim|scriptA> and <verbatim|scriptT>; article
    follows only the actual <verbatim|scriptT> factors required by the wire.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,95p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Signal.lean> \V
    signal/hinge definitions and the rail-chip transport identity.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,220p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Train.lean>,
    <verbatim|Bend.lean>, <verbatim|Chip.lean>, <verbatim|Reserve.lean>,
    <verbatim|Heart.lean>, <verbatim|Docked.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Moderate.lean> \V recursive cumulative-filter bounds,
    positivity, divisor, port, noise, pulse/vault, and cube-budget estimates.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,240p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Lines.lean> and
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,90p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Aliases.lean> \V
    one-dimensional box/rail estimates and alias coordinates.

    <item><verbatim|rg -n "lemma (flux_budget\|heart_budget\|tail_budget\|portD_budget\|notch_budget\|levy_budget\|sig_budget\|foot_budget\|brace_budget\|mouth_budget\|copper_budget\|stake_budget\|wire_budget\|honored\|propels\|differential_bound\|residue_cost\|traverse\|layout\|decay_cost\|matrix_cover\|tapes_sound\|issues)"
    Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS Lean/YM/Work/F07 Lean/YM/Laurent/Art.lean> \V
    located component producer declarations.
  </itemize-minus>

  No Lean or LaTeX build has been run for these edits. The required command
  <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and exited 1 because
  this isolated output directory has no <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>;
  adding shared unit metadata is outside the assigned outputs. The imported
  source revision was read from <verbatim|source/upstream.json>; no separate
  nested Lean checkout or alternate source revision is asserted. The
  component derivation status is recorded in
  <verbatim|free-kernel-components-evidence.md>.

